ORIGIN

This skill is original work. It was first distributed as one half of the "ambiguity-audit"
plugin, alongside the analysis skill now published as "ambiguity-stress-test" (originally
"interpretive-ambiguity-stress-test"). This release renders a completed audit; it does not
perform the analysis. The two are complementary but neither requires the other — this skill
accepts any structured or semi-structured ambiguity analysis, however produced.

---

BUNDLED CODE

Two Python renderers are included, scripts/generate_site.py and scripts/generate_latex.py.
Both target Python 3 and import only from the standard library (argparse, html, json, os,
pathlib, re, shutil, sys). Neither makes network calls, spawns subprocesses, evaluates
dynamic code, or writes outside the output directory named by the caller.

Generated websites reference Google Fonts by URL, so a rendered page loads those fonts from
an external service when opened in a browser. The font tokens in the spec can be overridden
with a local stack where that is unwanted.

